From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LIVI appliance
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_sync: ignore EINVAL from WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY

The Marlin (UWE5622/AW859A) controller on the Orange Pi Zero 2W reports
HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY (0x080f) as supported but answers the
command with Invalid HCI Command Parameters (-EINVAL) during HCI
initialisation. hci_init_stage_sync() treats any stage failure as fatal,
so the controller never finishes setup, the kernel never sends the mgmt
Index Added event, and BlueZ ends up with no adapter at all
("BlueZ never published /org/bluez/hci0" from livi-helperd).

The command only installs the default link policy (RSWITCH/HOLD/SNIFF/
PARK power-save modes), so dropping the error is safe. Armbian carries
the same workaround for this hardware (drv-net-bluetooth-hci-ignore-
def-link-policy-error.patch in its sunxi patch stack).
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -270,6 +270,13 @@
 		if (!event)
 			bt_dev_err(hdev, "Opcode 0x%4.4x failed: %ld", opcode,
 				   PTR_ERR(skb));
+
+		/* Ignore -22 for WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY - some controllers
+		 * report it as supported but reject it (e.g., Marlin/uwe5622)
+		 */
+		if (PTR_ERR(skb) == -EINVAL && opcode == 0x080f)
+			return 0;
+
 		return PTR_ERR(skb);
 	}
 
